# 
# Hook: Everyone runs agents in loops. Rysh puts the loop on a leash.
# Source: story-ad01-loop-leash.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:08.0]
Everyone is running agents in loops now. And everyone has the same fear: you walk away, and the loop runs away -- with your API bill. Rysh puts the loop on a leash.

[00:08.0 --> 00:24.0]
Any prompt becomes a reusable automation. Bind a page, save a recipe. It's a file on disk -- your automations live in git, not in a vendor's dashboard.

[00:24.0 --> 00:44.0]
Now the leash. Twenty pages -- rysh counts spend like reading: a page is a thousand tokens, two hundred pages make a book, twenty books a shelf. Twenty pages, ten minutes, hard ceilings. Not suggestions -- the run cannot outspend them.

[00:44.0 --> 00:56.0]
At eighty percent spent, the takeover prompt takes the wheel -- with the reserved twenty percent as its own budget -- to wrap up cleanly and save results. No clipped runs. No silent overspend. And status shows you the leash, live.

[00:56.0 --> 01:06.0]
When a pass ends, an LLM judge decides: goal fulfilled, the loop ends -- not yet, and it goes again. Stop it any time; continue resumes from the last checkpoint, budget re-armed. Interruptible by design.

[01:06.0 --> 01:12.0]
Schedule it. Cron takes any rysh input -- even whole automations. Headless, on a server, while you sleep.

[01:12.0 --> 01:19.0]
Agents that work while you sleep -- on a leash you define. rysh dot A I -- now onboarding design partners.

